ed", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le04ob03re6aud07", "type": "audio"}, {"content": "Kim, I feel so", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"content": "after an eighteen hour day.", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_7", "type": "objective"}]}, {"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "threw me for a loop", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 2, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le04ob03re6aud08", "type": "audio"}, {"content": "Your response to the e-mail", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"content": ".", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_7", "type": "objective"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 8, "template_override": 1}, {"type": "GIW", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nJulian asks Louise a series of questions about work.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: \n<span class=\"bullet\">Listen to the audio. </span> \n<span class=\"bullet\">Proofread the sentence. </span> \n<span class=\"bullet\">Click on the incorrect word. </span> \n<span class=\"bullet\">Type in the correct word to complete the sentence.</span>\n<span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary. </span>", "type": "text"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "are", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le04ob03re6aud09", "type": "audio"}, {"content": "You aren't still upset about what I said yesterday,", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "incorrect", "contents": [{"content": "isn't", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"content": "you?", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_8", "type": "objective"}]}, {"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "aren't", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le04ob03re6aud10", "type": "audio"}, {"content": "You're worried about the deal,", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "incorrect", "contents": [{"content": "doesn't", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"content": "you?", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_8", "type": "objective"}]}, {"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "isn't", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 2, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le04ob03re6aud11", "type": "audio"}, {"content": "Your boss is quite meticulous and organized,", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "incorrect", "contents": [{"content": "aren't", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"content": "she?", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_8", "type": "objective"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 9, "template_override": 1}, {"type": "RSLT", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 10, "template_override": 1}, {"type": "DWS", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Tell a friend what they should have done.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le04ob03re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}]}, {"type": "audio", "_data": [], "title": "", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "engenn9le04ob03re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Wow, Sally, you look drained. You're stressed out, aren't you?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yeah. What I really need is a vacation! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: What's going on? You aren't still rattled about what happened yesterday with your boss, are you?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: A little. It really threw me for a loop. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You really are sensitive, aren't you? Listen, what you need to do is talk to your boss about it. You need to have really open communication so that there are no misunderstandings.\nMake sure you ask lots of questions and be sure that other people understand you, too.", "image": "engenn9le04ob03re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: You're right. What I should do is schedule a meeting with my boss so we can discuss the variances in our communication styles.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Good idea! You need to have a face-to-face conversation, don't you? That you haven't spoken frankly with her yet is surprising. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: To be honest, I'm a little fearful of talking to her. She's really menacing sometimes.", "image": "engenn9le04ob03re2img05.jpg", "time": "35000", "id": 2}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Menacing! That's not right! Who you should really talk to is someone in human resources. Your boss is fairly new, isn't she? Maybe she needs some guidance on how to deal with her employees.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Okay. Tomorrow I'm going to meet with her and address the communication issues we have. If she's not open to discussing this with me, then I'll ask to speak to someone in human resources about her behavior.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sounds like a good plan. Good luck!", "image": "engenn9le04ob03re2img05.jpg", "time": "57000", "id": 3}], "coverimg": "engenn9le04ob03re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le04ob03re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "An Emotional Week", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "You're Too Sensitive", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Relate information about common solutions to problems.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements.<br/><br/> They are mainly used in speech when we want to:<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"strong\">confirm that something is true or not</span>, or</li> <li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a reply</span> from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes'.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A negative statement is followed by a positive question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no'.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were</span> you? </li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal</span> verb, the tag will be the same.<br/> For all other main verbs, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do/does</span> or <span class=\"italic\">did/didn't</span>.<br/><br/> Look at the examples in the chart:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/was't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wont you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You're stressed out, aren't you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You aren't still rattled about what happened yesterday with your boss, are you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " You really are sensitive, aren't you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You need to have a face-to-face conversation, don't you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Your boss is fairly new, isn't she? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "What Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You shift emphasis from the beginning to another part of the sentence by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> and <span class=\"italic\">who</span> phrases as subjects.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, you focus on the person doing the action in this case, the comedian telling jokes. <br/>   Example: <span class=\"italic\">John told a funny joke.</span><br/><br/> If we wish to place emphasis on another part of the sentence, we isolate that part and package up the rest of the information into a <span class=\"italic\">what</span>-phrase (or sometimes a <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause.)<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">What John said was funny.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">That</span> with a subordinated content clause can function as the subject of a sentence.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">That he imitated our teacher was funny.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">What</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Who</span> serves as a placeholder for the content of the noun phrase that has been moved to the end of the sentence. The effect is that more emphasis is placed on the initial content.<br/> Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What was hilarious was his imitation of the teacher.</span><br/>        <span class=\"italic\"> Who he should have made fun of was the principal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What I really need is a vacation! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What you need to do is talk to your boss about it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " What I should do is schedule a meeting with my boss.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That you haven't spoken frankly with her yet is surprising. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Who you really should talk to is someone in human resources.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "drained", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very tired", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Wow, Sally, you look drained.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about reactions and behavior in different situations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rattled", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to upset or disturb (someone)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You aren't still rattled about what happened yesterday?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to throw someone for a loop", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to confuse or surprise someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It really threw me for a loop. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "variance ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an amount of difference or change", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can discuss the variances in our communication styles.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "face-to-face", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in person; in the same location", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to have a face-to-face conversation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "frankly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in an honest and direct way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That you haven't spoken frankly with her yet is surprising. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fearful ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling fear", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm a little fearful of talking to her.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "menacing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who causes trouble or annoyance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  She's really menacing sometimes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Invent three things things that happened to you or three mistakes that you made.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell your partner the three things that happened to you and listen to his or her advice for what you should have done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Switch roles. Listen to what happened to your partner and give advice using <span class=\"italic\">should have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would have</span>.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about  reactions and behavior in a work situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for clarification and confirmation. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I shift emphasis by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">that</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give advice about what has happened.", "type": "text"}]}]}